      "class": "dataset",
      "label": "Purchase price of fuels for the  production of electricity and heat, and purchase price of received heat grouped by type of fuel. Year 2021-2025",
      "source": "Swedish Energy Administration",
      "updated": "2026-10-08T06:00:00Z",
      "link": {
        "related": [
          {
            "extension": {
              "relation": "statistics-homepage",
              "metaid": "PRODUCTCODE:EN0105"
            },
            "href": "https://www.scb.se/EN0105-en",
            "label": "Statistics page",
            "type": "text/html"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": [
        "Starting with reference year 2022, various kinds of wood waste are included in the category ”wood chips, wood waste, saw dust et al.”. Previous years, these have been included in the ”other fuels” category.",
        "Received heat from other sectors, mainly recovered waste heat from the manufacturing industry. ",
        "These statistics cannot be directly compared to statistics in Wood fuel and peat prices and Waste prices because of differences in methodology.",
        "The purchase prices for heat production exclude the heat production from the autoproducer CHP-plants.",
        "The purchase price is calculated for each type of fuel based on the average price of the purchases made during the year. The purchase value refers to the invoiced amount excluding VAT. Energy taxes, etc., that have been paid at an earlier stage may therefore be included in the price. However, energy taxes, etc., that have been paid directly by the reporting companies are not included.",
        "Starting with the reference year 2023, liquid biofuels (excl. black liquor, tall oil and pitch oil) are reported separately. In previous years this has been included in other fuels."
      ],
